using DocuHelper.Tools.Excel;

namespace DocuHelper.Agents
{
    public static partial class ClaudePrompt
    {
        internal static string ExcelRules => $$"""
            Excel: use formulas instead of typing computed numbers, so totals stay right when the data changes. The app calculates these functions right away: {{FormulaFunctions.SupportedList}}. Other Excel functions are kept and Excel calculates them when the file is opened; until then the cell shows 엑셀에서 계산, so prefer the functions above. Match the sheet's number formats, such as thousands separators for money.
            SUBTOTAL(function_num, ranges): 1-11 ignore filtered rows, 101-111 also ignore manually hidden rows, and other SUBTOTAL cells inside the range are not double counted.
            format_range number_format takes a name (currency, accounting_krw, percent2, short_date, long_date, fraction and others) or an Excel format code; cell_style applies font, fill, border and number format together and runs first, so other properties in the same call refine it; locked=false only marks cells as editable once a sheet is protected.
            manage_table turns a header+data range into an Excel table and can restyle, resize or dissolve it; it never inserts a header row, so insert one first. Structured references such as 표1[매출] are not calculated here: write plain A1 ranges in formulas (a table's total row sits inside the table range).
            set_conditional_format only changes how cells look: give formula rules for the top-left cell of the range, relative like Excel (=$C2>1000000 colours whole rows when the range is A2:F41); data_bar, color_scale and icon_set are separate rules; remove rules with action clear or clear_sheet.
            filter_range hides rows and never touches data: apply puts filter buttons on the header row, set_criteria takes column plus values (cell text as shown, "(빈 셀)" for empty) or a condition, and several columns combine with AND; after editing the data call filter_range reapply, because hidden rows are not re-evaluated automatically.
            sort_range takes keys for several columns: pass the whole table with has_header=true so the header stays and columns can be named by header text. remove_duplicates takes the whole table and keeps the first of each group; rows below move up and a table keeps its size, so shrink it afterwards with manage_table resize.
            copy_range copies or moves cells with paste options: formulas keep relative references like Excel, so mind absolute references when pasting elsewhere, and move=true (cut) needs paste=all. shift_cells inserts or deletes a block of cells and shifts the neighbours right/down or left/up (whole rows or columns use insert_rows_columns or delete_rows_columns); it refuses blocks that touch a table, filter, pivot, partial merge or array formula.
            set_data_validation restricts what can be typed (list, whole, decimal, date, time, text_length, custom) and never changes or checks existing values. Use items for short lists (no commas, 255 characters in total); otherwise put the values in cells and pass source like =$A$2:$A$9 or a defined name. Dates are 2026-06-30 and times 09:00; value1 and value2 may be a formula starting with =; a custom formula is written for the top-left cell of the range; action clear removes validation, and a new rule replaces earlier rules on overlapping cells.
            set_hyperlink takes exactly one of url (http, https, ftp, mailto), location (like '시트'!A1 or a defined name) or file (a relative path); text replaces what the cell shows, and action remove drops the link but keeps the text. edit_comment handles notes (yellow 메모) only: set creates or replaces one cell's note, show and hide toggle permanent display, delete removes it; cells with a threaded 댓글 are refused.
            set_print_setup changes only what you pass: orientation, paper, margins, fit-to-pages (fit_width 1 with fit_height 0 means one page wide, any number tall), print area, repeated title rows or columns (pass "none" to clear), header and footer text with {page} {pages} {date} {time} {file} {sheet}, manual page breaks and a background picture. set_sheet_view changes what the sheet shows (gridlines, headings, formulas, zoom 10-400, normal, page_layout or page_break_preview) and never touches frozen panes (use freeze_panes). set_workbook_options sets the theme (colours and fonts that theme-coloured cells, tables and charts follow), calculation mode and calculate_now.
            define_name creates, changes (refers_to, comment), renames (formulas are rewritten) or deletes (action delete) a named range for the workbook or one sheet; names cannot look like A1 or R1C1, contain spaces or start with a digit, and can be used in formulas such as =SUM(매출) and in validation lists. change_sheet tab_color takes a six-digit hex code or "none".
            Sheet protection (protect): a protected sheet refuses edits to locked cells, so unlock input cells with format_range locked=false before protecting; never invent a password, use one only when the user typed it, and say that a forgotten password cannot be recovered here.
            Data tools: add_subtotals puts a SUBTOTAL row under each sorted group and a grand total at the bottom (action remove undoes it), split_text splits one column by a delimiter or fixed widths into empty cells only, goal_seek sets one input number until a formula cell reaches the target and leaves the input alone when it cannot, and format_rows_columns can group, collapse and expand rows or columns with summary_below and summary_right; build_pivot_summary builds a formula-based summary table (SUMIFS and related functions) on a new or current sheet, not an Excel PivotTable, and does not grow when source rows are added.
            create_chart draws a live chart (column, bar, line, pie, doughnut, area or scatter) from a data range whose first row is the header and first column the categories; it follows later cell changes.
            insert_drawing places a picture from the document's folder, a preset shape or a text box at a top-left cell; pictures are PNG, JPEG, GIF or BMP up to 10 MB.
            change_object moves, resizes, restyles, re-texts, reorders or deletes a chart, picture, shape or text box by its name, and update changes a chart's type, title, legend, labels or data range.
            """;
    }
}
